WEBVTT

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:26.140
<i>I couldn't become like my mom.</i>

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.030
<i>What wasn't good enough?</i>

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.330
<i>Where did I go wrong?</i>

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:40.010
<i>If I can't use magical 
arts, then no one will...</i>

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:06.200
<b>Magic-Kyun Renaissance!</b>

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.990
The Sleeping Princess of the Frozen Forest

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.240
What? Um...

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:28.250
I'd like you to voluntarily drop out.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:31.500
Drop out? What are you talking about?

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:34.810
What did Aigasaki-senpai do?

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.760
If this is a joke, it's not funny.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.990
I wish it were a joke.

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.210
Look at those flowers.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.700
Aigasaki-san, it's clearly 
different from the Light of Arte

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.120
you previously produced.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.030
Yes.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.410
But, sometimes the shape can change.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.530
Yeah. Hana-chan-senpai's not the only one.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:11.540
However, they rarely become 
this snowflake shape.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.950
Students who produce light of this shape

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.130
are typically exceptionally talented

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.050
with an extraordinary sensitivity 
to the Light of Arte.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.980
Sensitivity to the Light of Arte?

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.770
So, Aigasaki...

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:34.940
And those students are likely to eventually 
destroy themselves with their art.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:38.580
Destroy themselves?

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.980
What does that mean?

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.450
It's exactly what it sounds like.

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:44.720
I've heard of it before.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.290
Some people devote themselves 
so wholly to the magical arts

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:50.080
that they lose themselves.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.250
I've heard of it, too.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.710
They're known as Destructive Artista.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.840
Ichijoji and Anjo are right.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.080
They become so engrossed in the magical arts

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.580
that they become unable to 
carry on with their real lives.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:06.240
In the worst cases,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:11.100
they even put their own lives in 
danger in exchange for their art.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:15.060
In order to prevent such a tragedy,

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:20.110
we recommend students who show 
dangerous symptoms to drop out.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:22.820
But what about Aigasaki's feelings?!

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.610
This is to protect Aigasaki-san.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:29.120
Aigasaki-san,

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:33.870
please refrain from using 
magical arts in the future.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:54.030
Sir, I don't think you 
needed to be so direct.

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:55.390
No.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:01.150
Trying to soften the blow 
would've been even more cruel.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.920
It's unfortunate.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.410
Oh, no...

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:14.750
Th-There's must be some kind of mistake.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.170
Hana-chan-senpai.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:22.170
After all, I'm not particularly 
talented or anything.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:26.930
I couldn't even produce 
sparkles before coming here.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:30.430
I'd never destroy myself 
or anything like that.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.070
I'd never...

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.850
Aigasaki.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.950
Yeah, it must be a mistake.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:40.310
The principal and Todo-sensei 
must be confused.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:44.360
Y-Yeah. You're probably just tired.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.820
You worked really hard 
during the Hoshi Festival.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:50.700
You'll be fine once you rest.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.770
You'll definitely be fine.

00:05:53.770 --> 00:05:56.830
There's no way you'd ever quit Hoshigei.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:01.090
Yeah. I'm going back to 
the dorms for the day.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:05.060
I need to rest well so I can 
be back to my usual self.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.200
Yeah, good idea.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.090
Yeah.

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:10.140
I'll go with you.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.710
I'll be fine.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:13.600
You should keep rehearsing.

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:14.100
But...

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:18.100
I'm going to do some thinking on my own.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:30.080
Hana-chan-senpai said she 
doesn't have any talent,

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.760
but that's not true.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.040
Yeah.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:37.370
No one could replicate the 
flower arrangements she makes.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:43.250
Yeah, and her sensitivity to the 
Light of Arte is exceptional.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:44.890
Hey, wait!

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:47.410
Are you saying the principal is right?!

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.170
Calm down, you two.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.990
We can't deny the possibility.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:52.680
What?

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:53.930
Senpai?

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:55.850
Ichijoji.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.480
Because we can't deny that possibility,

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.440
there's something we must do.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.310
We'll do everything we can to find a way

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:07.440
to restore Aigasaki's Light of Arte.

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:11.950
Senpai.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.790
We will save her.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.850
Teika's right.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.810
Yeah. Let's help her.

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.960
There's no way.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.970
Those students...

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:32.970
There's no way.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.970
...eventually destroy themselves with their art.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.470
There's no way.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.480
Once I rest, I'm sure I'll be back to normal.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.480
I'm sure I will be.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:49.090
After all, we have a 
Halloween event coming up.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:51.350
We're going to perform 
Sleeping Beauty together.

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:58.650
And there are lots of fun events like 
Christmas and New Year's after that, too.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:03.870
And we promised we'd be together forever.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:09.000
<i>And... and... and...</i>

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.240
Mom!

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.740
Mom!

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:40.490
Wait!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.000
Mom!

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:48.130
Mom!

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:54.590
Why?

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:57.010
Why is this happening?

00:09:01.460 --> 00:09:06.090
Mom, what did I do wrong?

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:11.860
All I did was try my best to be like you.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:14.920
Why?

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:20.710
Why do I have to quit Hoshigei?

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.620
Why?

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:27.810
No. I don't want to quit.

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:31.720
I'm going to be like you.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:36.100
No. I don't want this.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:47.390
Specially shaped Light of Arte.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:53.900
There must be previous cases 
and clues to curing it.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:03.910
Our library has one of the nation's largest 
collections of books on the magical arts.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:09.220
I'm sure we'll find a way to 
restore Senpai's Light of Arte.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:16.670
<b>Examples of the Hoshinomori School
 of Magical Arts' Light of Arte</b>

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:20.620
This is amazing.

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:23.470
It's packed with books.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:29.800
This room contains every document 
produced since Hoshigei opened.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:32.750
It's not open to regular students,

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.440
but we've made an exception for you.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:38.690
We may be able to find out what happened to 
students who suffered a fate similar to Aigasaki's—

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:44.200
Hana-chan-senpai.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.580
We'll definitely find something.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:56.840
Masana-niisan, Shinra-niisan, 
have you found anything?

00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:58.400
No.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:03.100
We've sent for documents from all over 
the world concerning the magical arts.

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:06.950
But only the recent ones have 
been added to the database.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:08.600
There just aren't enough samples.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:14.860
All we know right now is that a person's 
Light of Arte can change more than once.

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:15.730
Then...

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:18.310
<i>There's no guarantee it can be restored,</i>

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:20.650
<i>but it's worth looking into.</i>

00:11:21.810 --> 00:11:25.030
Add more people to the effort and 
broaden the scope of your research.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:25.670
Yes, sir.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:26.160
Teika.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.660
You should be with Aigasaki.

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:30.150
Brother...

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:36.340
<i>Almost every person whose Light of Arte 
took that shape became unstable.</i>

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.940
<i>If you leave her alone, 
she may never recover.</i>

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:41.680
Yes, brother.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:44.180
Kohana.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:46.280
Are you okay?

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:48.180
I brought cake.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.490
Kohana?

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:00.860
<i>I just need to produce the 
sparkles I used to make.</i>

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:04.240
<i>Then I can stay at Hoshigei.</i>

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:09.700
Aigasaki-san.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:13.460
Please refrain from using 
magical arts in the future.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.840
<i>But just once would be okay.</i>

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.010
<i>I have to try it.</i>

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:41.610
No.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.290
No. This isn't it. It's wrong.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.860
One more time.

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.870
That's it. It'll work this time.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.000
If I arrange them like this,

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:55.120
then I can produce my original sparkles.

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:02.720
Why?

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:06.230
Why? I'll do my best!

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:07.840
I'll work even harder!

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.100
So please...

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.350
Please let me produce my original sparkles.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:14.440
Please.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:18.360
Please, please, please, please.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.330
Aigasaki!

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.190
Did you find her?

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:57.270
No.

00:13:57.720 --> 00:13:59.330
Kohana...

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.860
I should've insisted on going back with her.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.340
What was that?

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:10.510
What happened?

00:14:10.510 --> 00:14:11.530
Could it be?

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:14.590
What's going on?

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:15.710
That was a really loud noise.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.100
We should call a teacher.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:18.690
Hey!

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:20.420
Wait! It's dangerous!

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:38.180
The Scala Artista...

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:39.330
But why?

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:43.180
I'm going to call a teacher.

00:14:49.770 --> 00:14:50.950
Aigasaki!

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:59.830
Magic-Kyun! Renaissance.

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.470
Thank you.

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:19.730
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:23.040
What's going on?

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:26.290
Medically speaking, there's 
nothing wrong with her.

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:29.740
She's just unconscious.

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:33.970
What happened?

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:39.600
There were signs that Aigasaki had been 
arranging flowers where she collapsed.

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:43.500
She may have been so worried that 
she closed off her own heart.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.000
If that's true,

00:15:46.770 --> 00:15:51.630
then Aigasaki won't wake up unless 
she's released from the cause.

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:53.190
No...

00:15:54.020 --> 00:15:55.640
This is my fault.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:58.910
I shouldn't have let her out of my sight.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:00.640
Kohana, wake up.

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:04.180
Senpai.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:05.400
Hana-chan-senpai.

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:07.840
Open your eyes.

00:16:07.840 --> 00:16:09.530
Hey, Aigasaki!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:11.540
My little flower.

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:14.230
Aigasaki.

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:33.910
It's cold. Where am I?

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:41.160
Mom.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.180
I'm disappointed in you.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:47.940
I thought you were going to become like me.

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:51.090
You couldn't do it.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:52.420
Mom.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:54.210
You can't do it anymore.

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:55.200
Mom!

00:16:55.730 --> 00:16:56.840
Mom?

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:00.950
You're not my child.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.210
W-Wait!

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:17.740
Teika-kun?

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:19.730
Stay away.

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:20.660
What?

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:23.220
You're my enemy.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.310
Teika-kun, why?

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:28.730
No, you're not even my enemy anymore.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:31.480
I have no business with failures.

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:35.800
T-Teika-kun.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:39.840
Teika-kun, I...

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:43.620
You're useless.

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:46.000
You're spineless.

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:48.500
Honestly, I'm disappointed.

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:51.500
You're just holding us back now.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.630
We'll find a new member for the committee.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.540
We don't need you anymore.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:00.140
W-Wait.

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:02.890
Wait!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.480
No! Let me in!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:10.400
I'll do my best! I'll do my best!

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.400
I'll work harder on my flower arrangements!

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:14.900
Look!

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.320
I'll use this flower to...

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:37.280
<i>I couldn't become like my mom.</i>

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.240
<i>What wasn't good enough?</i>

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:41.800
<i>Where did I go wrong?</i>

00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:44.990
<i>If I can't use magical arts,</i>

00:18:45.570 --> 00:18:47.300
<i>then no one will...</i>

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:49.660
<i>No one will...</i>

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:04.560
<i>Enough. I don't want to think 
about anything anymore.</i>

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:09.460
<i>Enough. I've had enough.</i>

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:11.450
<i>Enough...</i>

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:24.970
What is this?

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:25.970
Snow?

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:27.360
Kohana.

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:30.980
Her hands are cold.

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:33.250
They're like snow.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.410
My little flower.

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:36.980
Hang in there!

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:40.580
Yes. Yes, I understand.

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:42.490
No, excuse me.

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:49.000
The situation has become grave 
before we could find any clues.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:52.910
Since there's nothing that can 
be done for her medically,

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:55.380
there's no telling how 
long her body will last.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:19:59.440
Excuse me.

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:01.010
I see.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:05.350
Yes. No, thank you.

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:13.900
Kohana. Wake up, Kohana!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:17.860
Even though we found similar examples,

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:21.870
we still don't know how to 
restore her Light of Arte.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.740
Why? Why is this happening to Aigasaki?

00:20:31.220 --> 00:20:34.960
If Aigasaki were in our position,

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:37.710
she wouldn't give up.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:41.330
She would tell us with her smile,

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:43.470
"I know we can do it."

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:46.730
If I hadn't met Aigasaki,

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:51.470
I would still be living in a dark world.

00:20:51.820 --> 00:20:53.440
You're right.

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:56.630
If I hadn't met Aigasaki-san,

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:59.730
I wouldn't have known this world of light.

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.480
I would've been alone.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:07.490
I'm here with you guys 
because of Hana-chan-senpai.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.250
Yeah. If not for her,

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:12.750
we wouldn't have become friends.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:19.000
I'm still here at Hoshigei 
because of her encouragement.

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:24.260
She gave us something really precious.

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:27.540
Can you hear us?

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:31.390
Kohana, you can hear us, can't you?

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:35.110
So I won't give up.

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:38.900
Me neither.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:42.730
We all feel the same way.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:55.000
We'll never give up.

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:27.140
You're always positive.

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:28.240
And hardworking.

00:23:28.240 --> 00:23:29.760
And a little bit of an airhead.

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:31.310
But your heart is more beautiful.

00:23:31.310 --> 00:23:32.660
More noble than anyone else's.

00:23:32.660 --> 00:23:35.890
That's why we were drawn to you.

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:38.410
Next time on Magic-Kyun! Renaissance:

